+# N6 — prospective inspector dependency result
+
+**N6 is not release ready. No raw inspector, authority witness or product disclosure is implemented.** Existing source resolver contracts cannot supply the complete authority census required by the N5 prospective contract. This candidate uses the user's explicit missing-dependency fallback; it does not weaken inspection to a selected subset of events.
+
+The deliverable is a local committed dependency/test candidate: a source-backed audit, executable synthetic counterexamples, the smallest bounded resolver design, an explicit unimplemented route matrix and verification of the existing N5 behavior. It creates no new endpoint or permission. Ordinary Generate, moderation, acknowledgement and the admitted-job reader remain unchanged.
+
+The missing dependency is a resolver-owned, versioned complete census and requalification contract spanning source membership, original custody, owner/stream/project/document/revision binding, rights/lifetimes and excluded provenance. Snapshot equality, `source_event_refs`, cache high-water marks and the existing two-body custody helper do not provide it. The separate full-stream current-source diagnostic refuses ordinary worker preflight telemetry; filtering that history would violate its completeness boundary.
+
+N6 started in `/private/tmp/forma-n6-inspector`, branch `codex/forma-n6-inspector`, from exact N5 candidate `1091e3ef5dadc5854dcfa0382117180c9e73d2d5`. The release task's fresh authenticated remote-main check and its Production **542** receipt now confirm that same source commit; no rebase was needed. Direct N6 Git access returned HTTP403, so the source observation is attributed to that release task. Remote main must be reconciled again before any later release. N6 did not publish, and all 167 initially dirty original-checkout files retained their hashes.
+
+## Verification delivered
+
+**151 automated checks pass:** nine new executable dependency counterexamples, 72 existing focused regressions and 70 source/rebuilt Worker regressions. The build, TypeScript and changed-test lint pass. The browser review used the actual Still presenter and client with intercepted synthetic API responses: known item categories, unknown/legacy categories, inert markup and an unchanged request with explicit acknowledgement all behaved as expected. No acknowledgement or fixture job occurred merely from reading the warning. The final fixture created one synthetic job only after the explicit action.
+
+The automated browser driver is supplied but was not executed; the recorded browser review was performed through CUA at the normal desktop viewport. No N6 raw-inspection path exists to qualify. Every required N6 guard remains explicitly marked unimplemented/not run in the route matrix. The existing Worker tests and browser summary review must not be presented as N6 route certification.
+
+## Supported and unavailable
+
+N6 adds no supported raw inspection case. Even a small manual personal text-only preflight is unavailable until a complete prospective witness exists. Original/adopted, legacy, missing, expired, deleted/redacted, incomplete or out-of-scope source/body cases cannot gain access from this candidate. Longer raw retention never restores an expired preflight. No N4 source/body reconstruction, fabricated job or invented `GenerationRequested` sequence is attempted.
+
+Existing N5 summaries still report aggregate and per-item advisory results where recorded, with missing item categories unknown. They remain summaries, not verified body inspection. Existing explicit acknowledgement remains separate from reading the review.
+
+See [dependency and bounded design](dependency-design.md), [source audit](source-audit.md), [qualification matrix](qualification-matrix.json), [verification](verification.json) and [test manifest](test-manifest.json). Synthetic tests and browser review do not certify classifier quality, live custody, historical attribution or paid generation.
+
+**Next implementation dependency:** qualify the bounded census/requalification producer at the existing authoritative source resolver, then implement and run the full source/rebuilt Worker route and browser matrix. No provider call, paid trial, publication, policy/input/model/threshold change or N3/D2/I/J/L experiment is part of N6. Any live observation needs a separate exact proposal.
+
+[Progress Report](http://127.0.0.1:4187/) · [N5 contract](../n5/prospective-contract.md)
